{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_011Cf4zwkerDQZbVovtC8jos", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**One.**\n\nAll four lenses \u2014 ux, bugs, onboarding, content \u2014 score Mode A journey evidence, and lenses read a run folder rather than driving the browser themselves. One persona means one journey, so a single capture at https://example-nimbus-notes.test/app produces the screenshots, session log, timeline and observations that all four scorers then read in parallel.\n\nTraversal count scales with *modes \u00d7 personas \u00d7 sites*, not with lens count:\n- A second persona would add a second traversal.\n- A `technical` objective would add a Mode B measurement pass, and `seo`/`aeo` a Mode C crawl \u2014 different capture shapes, not re-drives of this one.\n- A competitor would add a full independent capture per site under Mode D.\n\nNone of those apply here, so: 1 traversal, 4 lenses over it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 8369, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11688, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 8369}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "391e7756-323a-4bb2-8de9-e97f1c0fcb92", "uuid": "63830f94-b61d-4873-8845-0f81ce56829c", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T09:37:12.349Z", "request_id": "req_011Cf4zwkBpHU18uJdw3Zurm"}
